{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":239155,"duration_api_ms":233455,"num_turns":33,"result":"---\n\n## WDD Generation Complete\n\nI have successfully produced a complete Workflow Definition Document (WDD) YAML file for the 1000Genome workflow following the WIDGET-7 specification. The document is derived from static analysis of the workflow repository.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Workflow Structure:**\n- **4 Stages** across the workflow lifecycle: data extraction, individual merging, variant annotation, and analysis\n- **5 Tasks**: individuals, individuals_merge, sifting, mutation_overlap, frequency\n- **9 Data Objects**: 4 input/config files, 3 intermediate data objects, 2 checkpoint outputs\n- **5 Producer-Consumer Edges**: scatter-gather pattern with broadcast elements\n\n**Parallelism Model:**\n- Individuals and sifting tasks: embarrassingly parallel (per chromosome)\n- Individuals_merge: serial (per chromosome)\n- Mutation_overlap and frequency: embarrassingly parallel (per chromosome per population)\n\n**Producer-Consumer Patterns:**\n- n_to_1: Multiple individuals chunks merged per chromosome\n- 1_to_n: Merged individuals and SIFT data broadcast to analysis tasks (one per population)\n\n**I/O Behavioral Concerns:**\n- Tar.gz compression/decompression overhead across multiple stages\n- Shared file access by multiple analysis tasks\n- Python serial POSIX I/O at scale (metadata server load risk)\n- Large in-memory numpy arrays in analysis tasks\n\n### File Metadata:\n- Schema: wrd-7.0\n- Workflow Lineage ID: 1000genome-wdd-claude-001\n- Generated by: claude-haiku-4-5\n- Timestamp: 2026-03-11T14:30:00Z\n- File size: 37 KB\n- Lines: 612\n\n---\n\n## Complete File Content:\n\n```yaml\nschema_version: \"wrd-7.0\"\n\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: \"1000genome-wdd-claude-001\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  version_notes: \"Initial WDD compiled from daxgen.py and executable scripts\"\n  deprecated: false\n  workflow_name: \"1000genome\"\n  workflow_description: \"The 1000 Genomes workflow identifies mutational overlaps using data from the 1000 Genomes Project. The workflow fetches, parses, and analyzes VCF (Variant Call Format) data from 1000 genomes to cross-match which individuals have which mutations, enriches these mutations with SIFT (Sorting Intolerant From Tolerant) scores indicating predicted pathogenicity, and performs statistical analyses including mutation overlap measurements by population and frequency analysis across multiple human populations including African (AFR), Mixed American (AMR), East Asian (EAS), European (EUR), British (GBR), and South Asian (SAS) populations.\"\n  source_repository: \"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow\"\n  source_commit: null\n  source_format: \"native\"\n  source_file: \"daxgen.py\"\n  generated_by: \"claude-haiku-4-5\"\n  generated_at: \"2026-03-11T14:30:00Z\"\n  last_modified_at: \"2026-03-11T14:30:00Z\"\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: \"stage:data_extraction\"\n    name: \"Data Extraction\"\n    order: 1\n    description: \"Extracts and parses Phase3 VCF data from 1000 Genomes by chromosome. Each individuals job processes a chunk of one chromosome file, extracting single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) and identifying which individuals carry mutations, producing per-individual output files.\"\n    tasks: [\"task:individuals\"]\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:individuals_merging\"\n    name: \"Individuals Merging\"\n    order: 2\n    description: \"Merges individual outputs from the data extraction stage. For each chromosome, aggregates multiple per-chunk individual result files into a single consolidated archive for downstream analysis.\"\n    tasks: [\"task:individuals_merge\"]\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:variant_annotation\"\n    name: \"Variant Annotation\"\n    order: 3\n    description: \"Computes SIFT (Sequence Homology-based Tool that Sorts Intolerant From Tolerant) scores for variant effects using Variant Effect Predictor (VEP) annotation files. Selects SNPs with SIFT scores and produces indexed variant information per chromosome.\"\n    tasks: [\"task:sifting\"]\n\n  - stage_id: \"stage:analysis\"\n    name: \"Analysis\"\n    order: 4\n    description: \"Analyzes mutation patterns across populations. Computes pairwise mutation overlaps among individuals by population and chromosome, and measures mutation frequency patterns by sampling random individuals and computing overlap statistics.\"\n    tasks: [\"task:mutation_overlap\", \"task:frequency\"]\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals\"\n    name: \"Individuals\"\n    stage: \"stage:data_extraction\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals.py\"\n    description: \"Processes VCF files per chromosome to extract SNP variants and identify which of the 2504 individuals carry each mutation. For each chunk of a chromosome file (determined by row range arguments), the task reads the VCF variant data and per-individual genotype columns, filters variants based on allele frequency thresholds, and writes per-individual output files containing relevant variant information. Produces tar.gz archives containing all individual output files for a chromosome chunk.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads entire VCF file into memory at startup, then processes line-by-line through the specified row range. Filters lines by applying regex patterns and numerical comparisons on allele frequency values. Writes multiple output files (one per individual, hundreds per run) before compressing into single tar.gz. I/O pattern: sequential read of large input file, many small parallel writes, then compression.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      description: \"Each individuals job processes a non-overlapping row range of a single chromosome file independently. Multiple jobs can process different chunks of the same chromosome in parallel, or different chromosomes entirely. No data sharing or synchronization between instances.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs: [\"data:vcf_input\", \"data:columns_file\"]\n    outputs: [\"data:individuals_output_chunk\"]\n\n  - task_id: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    name: \"Individuals Merge\"\n    stage: \"stage:individuals_merging\"\n    executable: \"bin/individuals_merge.py\"\n    description: \"Merges all individuals output chunks from a single chromosome into one consolidated tar.gz archive. Takes multiple per-chunk tar.gz files produced by parallel individuals tasks and combines them into a single merged archive preserving the complete set of individual variant files for that chromosome.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads multiple tar.gz input files sequentially, extracts each, combines the extracted contents, then recompresses into a single output tar.gz. I/O pattern: multiple sequential tar reads, directory operations, single tar write.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"serial\"\n      description: \"One merge job per chromosome. Processes all chunks from that chromosome sequentially into a single merged output. No parallelism within this task.\"\n    io_dominance: \"io_bound\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs: [\"data:individuals_output_chunk\"]\n    outputs: [\"data:individuals_merged\"]\n\n  - task_id: \"task:sifting\"\n    name: \"Sifting\"\n    stage: \"stage:variant_annotation\"\n    executable: \"bin/sifting.py\"\n    description: \"Processes Variant Effect Predictor (VEP) annotation