ses. I/O pattern: tar extraction, multiple array-based reads, random sampling in-memory, matplotlib I/O, final tar write.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      description: \"One job per chromosome per population. Each job independently computes frequency statistics for that population and chromosome. No dependencies between jobs.\"\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"checkpoint\"\n    inputs: [\"data:individuals_merged\", \"data:sifted_variants\", \"data:population_file\", \"data:columns_file\"]\n    outputs: [\"data:frequency_results\"]\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: \"data:vcf_input\"\n    name: \"VCF Input Files\"\n    description: \"Variant Call Format (VCF) files from the 1000 Genomes Phase3 release, one per chromosome. Each file contains approximately 250,000 lines of SNP variant data with genotype information for 2504 individuals. Format: tab-separated VCF with standard header lines (lines starting with '#') followed by variant records, where each column after position 9 represents one individual's genotype encoded as '0|0', '0|1', '1|0', or '1|1' indicating allele counts.\"\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"text\"\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n      datasets: []\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (10 files in test configuration, 22 for full genome)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"config_determined\"\n      controlling_parameter: \"datafile\"\n      config_file: \"data.csv\"\n      possible_values: \"integers 1-22 representing chromosome numbers; test config uses 1-10\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~250 MB per file (250,000 lines × ~1 KB per line)\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks: [\"task:individuals\"]\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"stage:data_extraction\"\n      last_consumer_phase: \"stage:data_extraction\"\n      retention_window: \"from external input to task:individuals completion\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"once\"\n      consumer_count: 1\n\n  - data_id: \"data:sift_annotation_vcf\"\n    name: \"SIFT Annotation VCF Files\"\n    description: \"Variant Effect Predictor (VEP) annotated VCF files containing SIFT pathogenicity predictions. One file per chromosome from the 1000 Genomes Project. Contains variant records with INFO field encoding SIFT scores and additional functional annotations in pipe-delimited format. Format: VCF with '#' header lines followed by variant rows, with INFO column containing structured annotations.\"\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"text\"\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n      datasets: []\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (10 files in test configuration, 22 for full genome)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"fixed\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~500 MB per file (larger than VCF due to annotation INFO fields)\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks: [\"task:sifting\"]\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"stage:variant_annotation\"\n      last_consumer_phase: \"stage:analysis\"\n      retention_window: \"from external input to task:frequency and task:mutation_overlap completion\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"few_times\"\n      consumer_count: 2\n\n  - data_id: \"data:individuals_output_chunk\"\n    name: \"Individuals Output Chunks\"\n    description: \"Tar.gz archives containing per-individual variant files produced by each individuals task. Each archive contains hundreds of individual files (one per person in that chunk), where each file lists the SNP variants (rs numbers and variant annotations) that individual carries with non-reference alleles meeting the allele frequency thresholds. Format: gzip-compressed tar archive of text files.\"\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"stage_scoped\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"tar\"\n      compression: \"gzip\"\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n      datasets: []\n    cardinality: \"multiple per chromosome (determined by -i/--individuals-jobs parameter; default 1, can be up to 250)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"config_determined\"\n      controlling_parameter: \"ind_jobs\"\n      config_file: \"daxgen.py\"\n      possible_values: \"integers 1-250; must evenly divide 250000 (default: 1)\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~50-150 MB per chunk (depends on allele frequency distribution; smaller chunks with higher ind_jobs)\"\n    producer_task: \"task:individuals\"\n    consumer_tasks: [\"task:individuals_merge\"]\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"stage:data_extraction\"\n      last_consumer_phase: \"stage:individuals_merging\"\n      retention_window: \"from task:individuals completion to task:individuals_merge completion\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"once\"\n      consumer_count: 1\n\n  - data_id: \"data:individuals_merged\"\n    name: \"Merged Individuals Files\"\n    description: \"Consolidated tar.gz archives containing all per-individual variant files for a single chromosome. Merges all chunks from parallel individuals tasks into one complete archive per chromosome. Format: gzip-compressed tar archive containing all individual variant files for that chromosome.\"\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"stage_scoped\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"tar\"\n      compression: \"gzip\"\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n      datasets: []\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (10 in test configuration, 22 for full genome)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"fixed\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~50-150 MB per chromosome (same total as input chunks but consolidated)\"\n    producer_task: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer_tasks: [\"task:mutation_overlap\", \"task:frequency\"]\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"stage:individuals_merging\"\n      last_consumer_phase: \"stage:analysis\"\n      retention_window: \"from task:individuals_merge completion to task:mutation_overlap and task:frequency completion\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"few_times\"\n      consumer_count: 2\n\n  - data_id: \"data:sifted_variants\"\n    name: \"Sifted Variants\"\n    description: \"Tabular text files containing filtered SNP variants with SIFT pathogenicity scores. One file per chromosome. Each line contains: variant line number, rs identifier, ENSEMBL gene ID, SIFT score, and phenotype prediction, extracted from VEP annotations. Format: space-delimited text with one variant per line.\"\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"stage_scoped\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"text\"\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n      datasets: []\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (10 in test configuration, 22 for full genome)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"fixed\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~1-10 MB per chromosome (only variants with SIFT scores, typically 1-5% of all variants)\"\n    producer_task: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer_tasks: [\"task:mutation_overlap\", \"task:frequency\"]\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"stage:variant_annotation\"\n      last_consumer_phase: \"stage:analysis\"\n      retention_window: \"from task:sifting completion to task:mutation_overlap and task:frequency completion\"\n 